3. PC Brain Layer — server.py + jarvis_brain.py
3.1 WebSocket Bridge — server.py 
server

Responsibilities:

Listen on WebSocket port 8765.

On client connect, instantiate a JARVISBrain() and stay attached.

Handle two message types from Pi:

simple_local_reply

Payload: { "text": "<final answer string>" }

Behaviour:

Call brain.generate_audio(text) to get Fable MP3 bytes.

Stream them to Pi as tts_chunk + tts_end.

chat

Payload: { "text": "<user query transcript>" }

Behaviour:

Call brain.process_text_input(text) → full LLM response string.

Call brain.generate_audio(response_text) → Fable audio.

Stream audio as above.

It does not:

Decide on intents.

Talk to Google APIs.

Manage HUD; it is purely a bridge.

3.2 Intelligence Core — jarvis_brain.py (JARVISBrain) 
jarvis_brain

Role: “PC Intelligence Core”, running under WSL2 with GPU.

Models
LLM / GPT:

Uses Ollama Llama3 through the OpenAI-compatible HTTP endpoint:

base_url='http://localhost:11434/v1'

model='llama3'

This means all reasoning is local, no remote GPT cost.

TTS voice:

Uses a separate OpenAI OpenAI() client:

model='tts-1'

voice='fable'

That is the premium Jarvis voice.

Personality & Memory
Imports and uses:

PersonalityEngine — system prompt + safety filtering.

JARVISMemory — long-term memory in ~/JARVIS/runtime/memory.

ContextManager — builds XML context for the model.

ProactiveSuggestionEngine — adds optional suggestions.

Time Handling
Detects time queries with regex (what time is it, what’s the time, etc.).

For time queries:

Compute Europe/London time via ZoneInfo("Europe/London").

Produce answer like:

“The current time in Kent, UK is hh:mm am/pm, Sir.”

Does not call LLaMA3 for time; fully local.

General Query Flow
Input text arrives from Pi (chat case).

Dangerous input is filtered / sanitised.

Check for TIME intent; respond locally if matched.

Build system prompt:

Personality,

System info (OS, hostname, etc.),

“SYSTEM DATETIME” explicit ground truth.

Add dynamic context XML from memory.

Call LLaMA3 via Ollama with the combined messages.

Append proactive suggestion if any.

Save conversation to memory DB.

Return final answer string to server.py.

TTS
generate_audio(text):

Calls OpenAI TTS tts-1 with voice fable.

Returns raw audio bytes.

Errors logged and reported.

